/opt/homebrew/bin/gitleaks
usage: scan_env_history_secrets.py [-h] [--repo REPO] [--env-file ENV_FILES]
                                   [--json-output JSON_OUTPUT]
                                   [--max-findings MAX_FINDINGS]
                                   [--allow-findings]

Scan Git history for secret-like assignments in runtime .env files. The
scanner never prints secret values. It reports commit, path, line number, key
name, value length, and a short hash fingerprint for triage.

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --repo REPO           Repository path
  --env-file ENV_FILES  Runtime env basename to scan; repeatable. Defaults to
                        known runtime env names.
  --json-output JSON_OUTPUT
                        Write full redacted JSON findings
  --max-findings MAX_FINDINGS
                        Max text sample findings
  --allow-findings      Exit 0 even when findings are present
